      "shloka_number": 1,
      "full_sanskrit": "हंसं नारायणं चैवमेतन्नामाष्टकं पठेत् ॥ १॥",
      "sandhi_split_sanskrit": "हंसं नारायणं चैवमेतन्नामाष्टकं पठेत् ॥ १॥",
      "iast_transliteration": "acyutaṃ keśavaṃ viṣṇuṃ hariṃ satyaṃ janārdanam .\nhaṃsaṃ nārāyaṇaṃ caivametannāmāṣṭakaṃ paṭhet ..1..",
      "meaning_english": "One should recite this octad of divine names: Achyuta (the Imperishable), Keshava (the Lord with beautiful hair), Vishnu (the All-Pervading), Hari (the Remover of sins), Satya (the Truth), Janardana (the Refuge of all beings), Hamsa (the Supreme Swan), and Narayana (the Abode of all souls).",
