      "shloka_number": 2,
      "full_sanskrit": "शत्रुसैन्यं क्षयं याति दुःस्वप्नः सुखदो भवेत् ॥ २॥",
      "sandhi_split_sanskrit": "शत्रुसैन्यं क्षयं याति दुःस्वप्नः सुखदो भवेत् ॥ २॥",
      "iast_transliteration": "trisandhyaṃ yaḥ paṭhennityaṃ dāridryaṃ tasya naśyati .\nśatrusainyaṃ kṣayaṃ yāti duḥsvapnaḥ sukhado bhavet ..2..",
      "meaning_english": "One who recites this hymn daily at the three junctures of dawn, noon, and dusk — their poverty is destroyed. The armies of enemies perish, and even bad dreams become bestowers of happiness.",
