    {
      "shloka_number": 3,
      "full_sanskrit": "ब्रह्मविद्याप्रबोधश्च तस्मान्नित्यं पठेन्नरः ॥",
      "sandhi_split_sanskrit": "ब्रह्मविद्याप्रबोधश्च तस्मान्नित्यं पठेन्नरः ॥",
      "iast_transliteration": "gaṅgāyāṃ maraṇaṃ caiva dṛḍhā bhaktistu keśave .\nbrahmavidyāprabodhaśca tasmānnityaṃ paṭhennaraḥ ..3..",
      "meaning_english": "Death upon the banks of the Ganga, steadfast devotion to Keshava, and the awakening of knowledge of Brahman — for these blessings, one should recite this hymn daily. Thus concludes the sacred Ashtakam of the eight names of Lord Vishnu, complete in its entirety.",
